'''Greed mode''' is a game mode introduced in ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth]]''.

== Gameplay ==
[[file:Greed Mode Layout.png|125px|right]]
In Greed mode, each floor has a {{R|Curse Room}}, a {{R|Devil Room}}/{{R|Angel Room}}, a double-wide [[#Shop|Shop]], and an exit room all connected to a main double-height arena room with a [[button]] in the center. A {{R|Super Secret Room}} is also connected to one of the rooms. Up until the penultimate floor, an already unlocked {{R|Treasure Room}} with a silver door frame and a normal locked Treasure Room are also available. The silver Treasure Room always gives items from the [[Boss (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Boss pool]]. The sixth floor (The Shop) does not have any Treasure Rooms but does have the Shop and Curse Rooms. The final seventh floor has no waves and contains only three rooms, the largest of which contains the game mode's [[Ultra Greed|final boss]].

When playing Greed Mode, a yellow coin ({{mode|greed}}) will appear on the [[HUD]], below the consumables.

=== Shop ===
As there are no normal drops in Greed mode, the Shop becomes Isaac's primary source of items and pickups. Shops in Greed mode automatically restock. Shops will always have six items/pickups for sale, sometimes discounted; in order from the left side of the room to the right, these will always be:
* A {{e|Key}}
* A [[Hearts|red heart]]
* A [[Shop (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Shop item]]
* A [[Boss (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Boss item]]
* Two random pickups, [[trinkets]], or items from the [[Treasure Room (Greed Mode Item Pool)|Treasure Room pool]].
There will also almost always be two {{e|Shopkeeper}}s near the center of the room, as sometimes just one special shopkeeper spawns instead.

