=== Arena ===
The 1x2 room in the center of all floors except the final one is the Arena, where most of the game mode's coins and enemies come from.  These rooms always have a [[button]] in the center that, when pressed, bars all the doors and starts spawning waves of enemies and coins. While active, the button has a timer underneath it that counts down; when the timer runs out or all enemies in the current wave are killed, the next wave spawns. This continues until wave 8 or 10 is reached, Isaac dies, teleports out of the arena or presses the button again. Pressing the button before all the waves have spawned deals half a heart of damage to Isaac (or removes 1 penny from the next wave if playing as {{C|The Lost}} or {{C|Tainted Lost}}) and stops the timer that causes waves to spawn automatically. Once the timer stops and all remaining enemies are killed, the doors re-open. The button can then be reactivated to continue progressing through the waves. Once all waves are spawned, the button's spikes retract and cannot be pressed until all enemies are cleared. All waves except the optional "nightmare" wave must be completed for the door to the next floor to open.

For the first 8 waves, the timer will start at a set time and then increase by 1 second for subsequent waves. For {{s|Basement}} and {{s|Caves}}, the clock starts at 6 seconds. For {{s|Depths}}, the clock starts at 5 seconds. For {{s|Womb}}, the clock starts at 4 seconds. For {{s|Sheol}} and {{s|The Shop}}, the clock starts back at 6 seconds again. The first boss wave is set at 33 seconds (30 after {{a|Everything is Terrible 2!!!}} is unlocked) on all floors.

The enemies spawned by each wave are determined by the wave number and current floor. Each wave is as follows:
* Normal enemy waves:
** Wave 1-3: "Easy" enemy pool
** Wave 4-6: "Medium" enemy pool
** Wave 7-8: "Hard" enemy pool 
* Boss waves:
** Wave 9: "Easy boss" pool 
** Wave 10: "Medium boss" pool
* Wave 11 (optional): Nightmare boss wave - "Hard boss" pool (spawns the floor's {{R|Devil Room}}/{{R|Angel Room}} on completion).

Note that "boss" pools can include multiple (mini)bosses spread out across the room. Unlike normal mode, deal chances will only appear after doing the extra wave, and their spawn chances are not affected by taking red heart damage.

{{dlc|r}} Enemies can spawn as [[Monster#Champions|Champions]] as normal, but will not drop pickups, with the exception of {{E|The Hollow}}'s gold champion, which drops coins as normal. Rainbow champions drop consumables too, albeit only appear in Sheol in {{mode|greed|greedier}} Greedier version of the mode.

At the start of each wave, Pennies are dropped on the ground, which Isaac can use in the [[#Shop|Shop]] to purchase items and pickups. Each normal wave drops 2 pennies, each boss wave drops 4 pennies along with a bonus coin after passing through 3 waves without receiving red heart damage. That means on a full hitless floor, an extra coin can be obtained on waves 4, 7 and 10, bringing the total of coins earned to 27 per floor. This extra coin mechanic explains why sometimes a coin can spawn on the 11th wave.

Each new wave counts as a new 'room' for purposes of item charges, familiars dropping items or the like. However, one-room temporary effects, such as {{i|The Book of Belial}}, will remain across waves, and items that activate upon entering a new room will not activate when a new wave starts.
* {{i|Taurus|r}} is an exception and will activate each time the button is pressed to start a wave.

