== Tips ==
* Flight will not prevent damage from the spiked stop button unless the player is {{C|The Lost}}, {{C|Tainted Lost}}, or {{C|Tainted Forgotten}}.
** However, a Penny is deducted from the next round of rewards if the button is pressed as {{C|The Lost}} or {{C|Tainted Lost}}. It is possible to negate this by triggering the button and surviving until all waves have spawned before quitting out. When reloading the save, all of the coins will be on the ground. Pressing the button again will start the waves from wave 1, but will no longer spawn coins, removing the downside.
* Items with effects that only persist in the room are especially useful in Greed mode. Complete all waves in one go to maximize their efficiency. Examples of such items include {{i|Box of Friends}}, {{i|The Book of Belial}}, {{i|The Nail}}, {{i|Lusty Blood}}, {{i|The Pinking Shears}}, {{i|Scissors}}, and {{i|Sulfur}}.
* Being teleported by the Curse of the Maze can open the exit door without needing to complete the floor, allowing large portions of a run to be skipped.
* Only a half heart of damage is taken in floors beyond chapter 3, a feature unique to Greed mode.
** This makes items such as {{i|The Wafer}} substantially less useful, since there is a limited number of enemies that could cause more than a half heart of damage. However, they can still be used for the Ultra Greed boss fight, since all of his attacks deal a full heart of damage.
* Killing all the enemies before the timer resets doesn't increase the number of coins produced.
* It is also often a good idea to get rid of pickups on the ground if possible, as they can limit movement in a relatively cramped arena.
* Due to the fact that the mode presents fewer rocks, finding {{r|Crawl Space}}s is much easier.
* Using keys or bombs to open golden and stone chests is almost always worth it since it's highly likely that it will return the used pickup, with the smaller possibility of an item like the {{I|A Quarter}}.
* Staying towards the middle of the room makes seeing most of the arena at once, as well as avoiding potential instant damage.
* It is often a good idea to press the button when the arena is flooded by invulnerable entities like {{e|Death's Head}}s or {{e|Poky||Pokies}}, so that they are guaranteed to die once the waves are complete. Clearing the room before the next wave still deactivates them.
* Firing non-stop is not always the wisest thing to do as it can lead to instant damage, from something like explosions for example. Items like {{I|Cursed Eye}} and {{I|Chocolate Milk}} help avoiding that, although Cursed Eye is still a double edged sword.
* "The Shop" penultimate chapter often spawns several shopkeeper entities throughout the waves, which can be blown up for extra cash.
* The shop keepers have a very low chance of dropping {{i|Steam Sale}} or {{T|Counterfeit Penny}} and other useful pickups when bombed.
* Sometimes spending the acquired pennies may be wiser on the next floor. Certain collectible items, hearts or keys may be on sale a depth below, which saves money compared to refilling them when not yet necessary.
* Any form of homing is tremendous in this gamemode as its' effect covers a relatively large part of the arena.
* {{dlc|r}} "Ace of" cards are very helpful to use on spawning enemies — be it to heal up or gain resources.
* {{I|Sack Head}} tends to replace the coins {{E|Ultra Greedier}}'s coin explosions spawn, which can be useful for{{C|Tainted Lost}} with a clutch {{P|Holy Card}}. Alternatively - it could be useful for battery drops instead.
* There are methods of achieving infinite coins/items. Although difficult to coordinate, and sometimes heavily reliant on luck, these methods can practically guarantee a successful run. These strategies can be combined with {{i|Chaos}} to allow stronger items to be obtained more easily.
** Method #1: Requires a {{P|2 of Diamonds}} card, the {{i|Blank Card}}, a Shop selling {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}}, and enough coins to buy one. This allows infinite coin count doubling with no drawback.
** Method #2: Requires {{P|Jera}}, the {{i|Blank Card}}, a Shop selling {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}}, and enough coins to buy one. Similar to the first method, but instead of doubling Isaac's currently held coins, this method allows for infinite duplication of Pennies dropped during waves.
*** {{dlc+|r}} Since {{i|Blank Card}} no longer copies the ability of the runes, this method no longer works with {{P|Jera}}, so instead you need {{i|Clear Rune}} in place of {{i|Blank Card}}, a Shop selling {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}}, and enough coins to buy two, as Clear Rune requires 12 charges to copy effect of {{P|Jera}}.{{dlc-}}
** Method #3: Use {{i|Diplopia}} or the {{i|Crooked Penny}} on a {{i|Steam Sale}}. This will allow Isaac to take as many items as desired for free.
*** {{dlc|r}} This method is no longer infinite, as stacking multiple {{i|Steam Sale}} uses a new algorithm.
** Method #4: Requires {{T|Swallowed Penny}} and a discounted red heart (2c). Use the curse door by entering and exiting right after losing only half a red heart and spawning a coin. By repeating the process long enough you can get infinite coins, {{T|Swallowed Penny}} being able to spawn nickels and dimes and being guaranteed 1 penny per half heart. If {{I|Mom's Box}} is held, this method can be performed without a discounted red heart as the number of coins spawned by {{T|Swallowed Penny}} will be doubled.
* The {{i|D20}} can be used in tandem with {{E|Lil' Battery|text=Lil' Batteries}} to re-roll all Pennies dropped during combat, some of which will become Grab Bags or chests. The process can then be repeated indefinitely.
** {{dlc|nr}} As the D20 re-rolls all opened chests into pickups, chests should not be opened unless the D20 is fully charged.
** {{dlc+|r}} Using the D20 in conjunction with the {{i|Book of Virtues}} will destroy all pickups in the room; as such, the D20 should not be picked up while playing as {{C|Bethany}}.{{dlc-}}
** This method also works with {{i|D infinity}} or {{i|Clear Rune}} paired with a {{p|Soul of Eden}}.
* {{dlc|nr}} In Greedier mode, upon defeating Ultra Greedier, all poops, whether destroyed, damaged or intact, will be converted into {{E|Golden Poop}}s.
** As a result, {{P|A Card Against Humanity}} can be used to guarantee a large source of coins for the Greed Donation Machine.
*** {{Dlc|r}} Poops spawned inside of the Ultra Greedier fight are turned into yellow colored poops, and drop normal brown poop pickups.
* Common display resolutions, such as 1920x1080 with aspect ratio 16:9, will show only part of the arena in fullscreen mode. Switching to windowed mode and then resizing the window makes it possible to keep an eye on the entire arena while playing.

=== Helpful Items ===
As mentioned above, all items that grant a temporary buff or benefit that expire once Isaac leaves the room are extremely powerful in Greed Mode, as these effects can last an entire floor's worth of waves, and some can be stacked. Items typically useful in Normal Mode that are not enhanced by Greed Mode's nature are not listed.

* {{I|Steam Sale}}: Reduces prices so that more items can be bought, and saves more money for the Greed Machine.
* {{I|Sack of Pennies}} / {{I|A Quarter}} / {{I|A Dollar}}: Provides an abundance of money.
* {{I|Mystery Sack}} / {{I|Sack of Sacks}} / {{i|Bomb Bag}}: Provides more pickups, especially bombs which are scarcer in Greed Mode.
* {{I|Keeper's Sack}}: Due to the gamemode's nature, many stats ups will be granted by this item very frequently.
* {{I|Leech}} / {{I|Charm of the Vampire}}: The large amount of enemies means more healing.
* {{I|Crooked Penny}}: May be used to duplicate all shop contents. If Crooked Penny fails, the shop could simply be rerolled to replenish its contents.
* {{I|Linger Bean}}: Any cloud created by the item stays afloat for a while & provides a consistent, wide-area effect.
* {{I|Brown Nugget|r}}: Multiple flies can be spawned in the arena before starting the waves.
* {{I|Akeldama}}: Slows down and damages chasing enemies, who can get overwhelming as the waves get shorter.
* {{I|Lemon Mishap}} / {{I|Free Lemonade}}: Deals great AoE damage.
** {{dlc|r+}} Creep created by '''Lemon Mishap''' remains on the ground indefinitely, allowing Isaac to cover a large portion of the room in it.
* {{I|Sprinkler}}: Can be used multiple times in one arena.
* {{I|Gnawed Leaf}}: Allows for passive damage through familiars while staying invincible.
* {{I|Mega Blast}} / {{I|Mega Mush}}: Long lasting effects that can trivialize a floor.
* {{I|Plum Flute}}: Baby Plum is able to damage way more enemies as they are usually strewn about in the room.
* {{I|Star of Bethlehem}}: Always present in the middle of arena, allowing for great DPS increase, though it also makes accidentally pushing the button easier.
* {{I|Red Stew}}: The damage buff can be sustained by the constant onslaught of enemies.
* {{I|The Stairway}}: As long as one remains in the arena at the start of a floor, the ladder won't disappear. This allows Isaac to get richer before going into The Stairway's deal.
* {{I|Quints}}: Gives you a persistent source of help during all the waves.
* {{I|Jar of Flies}}: The high enemy count of Greed Mode causes Jar of Flies to generate stacks very quickly.
* {{I|Ocular Rift}} / {{I|Lodestone}} / {{I|Black Hole}}: Can suck up many enemies in large chunks garnered in close proximity.
* {{I|Hungry Soul}}: Very useful in a run since massive formation of enemies are ever-present throughout.
* {{I|Purgatory}}: Can be timed to fire a ghost right as a new wave generates.
* {{I|It Hurts}}: The effects stack throughout the entire arena zone.
* {{i|Azazel's Rage}}: Triggers every 4 waves and can easily wipe out every enemy in the arena.
* {{I|Larynx}}: Cleans up the enemies fast as well as preventing hits with high likelihood.
* {{I|D10|r}}: Downgrades all the enemies in the room, useful because of the low charge amount.
* {{i|Birthright}} + {{c|Tainted Cain}}: Purchasing an on-sale item over and over while having Birthright results in almost infinite consumables.
* {{i|Betrayal|nr}}: Charms every enemy when hit, allowing an entire wave to be cleared at the cost of one hit.
* {{I|Betrayal|dlc=r}}: The high enemy count will cause them to harm each other more often.
* {{I|The Candle}}: Can be used to wipe out clusters of enemies, which helps prevent overcrowding.
* {{I|Black Candle}}: While most curses don't especially matter in Greed Mode, Curse of the Blind is especially devastating, making immunity to it very valuable.
* {{I|Paschal Candle}}: Quickly gains stacks, especially later on, due to the short wave timer.
* {{I|Midas' Touch}} + {{I|E. Coli}}: Touching enemies turns them into golden poops, making you rich.
* {{I|Cube of Meat}} / {{I|Ball of Bandages}},{{I|Mom's Heels}},{{I|The Virus}},{{I|Serpent's Kiss|dlc=a}}, {{I|Aries}}, {{I|Little Horn}}, {{I|The Nail}} and {{I|My Shadow|r}}: Since the mode prevents telefragging for a tiny amount of time even if enemies spawn on top of you - the contact damage trait of that item becomes very useful to instantly kill those that spawn on you with no consequences, however it can turn out badly if said monsters are explosive.
* {{I|Keeper's Kin}}: Provides support in early floors due to the abundance of rocks.
* {{I|Glass Cannon}}: helps immensely with clearing waves, it's possible to even use it in advance before pressing the buttons to get use of 2 shots in a row.
* {{I|Potato Peeler}}: Meat boys can be created in mass due to the abundance of HP ups available in the shop. Isaac also emits damaging creep for the current room after using the item.
* {{i|Book of the Dead}}: Spawns bone orbitals or charmed {{E|Bony|text=Bonies}} when there are killed enemies in a room. Making this item especially useful after the first 8 rounds and before the boss rounds.
* {{i|D20}}: The D20 is a one-item game breaker as long as the Shop has a {{e|Lil' Battery}} available. See the tips section above for more information.
* {{i|D infinity|r}}: Incredibly powerful in Greed Mode, as the dice can now be toggled to mimic the effects of the {{i|D1}}, {{i|The D6}}, and the {{i|D20}}, allowing Isaac to quickly gain consumables and reroll items.
* {{i|Dark Arts}}: Dark Arts can be used to press the button without taking any damage, kill many enemies with each activation, and have the item be constantly recharged with each wave.
** While playing as {{C|Tainted Judas}}, each enemy or projectile ran into will grant a damage buff. With the sheer amount of enemies appearing, especially in Greedier, Tainted Judas will gain an immense damage buff and can kill huge swaths of enemies with ease. Additionally, this is even more potent against {{E|Ultra Greed}}, as you can run through the many {{E|Greed Gaper}}s summoned to gain even greater damage buff, as the Gapers will be clustered very closely together.
* {{i|Gello}}: Incredibly powerful, as it can be activated multiple times in the same room.
* {{I|Hemoptysis}}: Can be spammed to push into enemies into walls, which happens almost always due to the arena being somewhat secluded.
* {{i|No. 2}}: Can deal room-wide damage every 5 seconds, as well as giving you free bombs to blow up shopkeepers & secret room walls.
* {{i|Red Candle|nr}}: Filling the room with flames before pushing the button will quickly kill all enemies and bosses.
** {{Dlc|r}} This method is no longer effective because the flames now extinguish after a set time.
* {{i|Wooden Nickel}}: Allows for an easy gain for a lot more money very quickly, as it can be used once per wave. If the {{i|9 Volt}} is also picked up, Isaac can use activate the item once every 15 seconds to gain infinite money as long as there is an enemy left in the room.
* {{T|Liberty Cap}}: Can be used to repeatedly exit and re-enter the arena to force the {{i|Magic Mushroom}} effect.
* {{T|Mom's Lock}}: Can be used to repeatedly exit and re-enter the arena to force the {{i|Mom's Knife}} effect.
* {{T|Counterfeit Penny}}, {{T|Swallowed Penny}} and all other penny trinkets are useful due to the nature of Greed Mode. Even {{T|Cursed Penny}} is useful if you're trying to teleport into the exit door of the floor; Although it is wise to take all money before picking the trinket up, and only using it with 1 coin left.
* {{T|Equality!|nr+}}: With careful pickup management, the coins can be doubled.
* {{T|Eve's Bird Foot}}: The bird provides consistent help throughout waves.
* {{T|Samson's Lock}}: Abundance of enemies offers consistent damage increase.
* {{p|Berkano|r+}}: Consistently useful in Greed Mode due to locusts lasting as long as Isaac stays withing the arena.
* {{T|Sigil of Baphomet}}: The wave based enemy spawns allow for constant uptime.
* {{i|Coupon}}: Can be used to make pickups or items free in the shop, in exchange for making them no longer restock. Can also be used to take Devil Deals for free, conserving any heart containers, which are more valuable due to red heart damage having no effect on Deal chances.

=== Unhelpful Items ===
* {{i|Blanket}}: Only grants a shield for the two boss fights on the final level. The shield does not activate for the regular boss waves on previous floors.
* {{i|Camo Undies|a+nr}}: This item does almost nothing in Greed Mode, despite being able to be obtained from the Greed Mode Treasure Room.
** {{dlc|r}} Due to its ability to destroy {{e|Shopkeeper}}s, Camo Undies can net you some extra pennies or nickels from shops each floor. Its new effect in Repentance also nets you a risk-reward dynamic as long as you re-enter the arena. You risk by losing money but get rewarded by clearing the waves easier.
* {{i|Champion Belt}}:While it does provide a damage up, it also quadruples the chance for champion enemies to appear, while not being able to profit from any extra pickups dropping from champions.
* {{i|D12}}: Very few rocks to reroll, however, can be abused to force a hatch to the next floor.
* {{i|Eucharist}}: You're already guaranteed an Angel or Devil deal each floor, so all this does is ensures that it's an Angel Deal.
* {{i|Guppy's Eye}}: This item is substantially less useful in Greed Mode, due to the scarcity of chests.
* {{i|Guppy's Tail}}: This item has no effect in Greed Mode other than counting towards the Guppy Transformation.
* {{i|Holy Mantle}}: Only triggers once without leaving the room, however can still be useful to make use of curse rooms for free; As well as deactivating the wave button with no consequences.
* {{I|Monstro's Tooth}}: Only targets one enemy, virtually useless with the exception of cleaning up dead shopkeeper bodies.
* {{i|Mom's Bracelet}}: Very few rocks to throw.
* {{i|Mama Mega!}}: The explosion will only trigger once per room, making it effectively useless in Greed Mode after the first activation.
* {{i|The Mind}}: In Greed Mode, this item effectively becomes {{i|Blue Map}}. Other map-related items such as {{I|Treasure Map}} and {{I|The Compass}} are negated completely irrelevant.
* {{i|Pause}}: Using the item in Greed Mode will freeze all enemies but will not pause the timer. New waves of enemies will continue to spawn even while the effect is active.
* {{p|Soul of Cain}}: Will show red door outlines, but cannot generate normal red rooms, leaving only special rooms as a rare possibility. The red outlines can be used to find the Secret Room or leave the floor, however.
* {{I|Meat Cleaver|dlc=r}}: Virtually useless, especially considering how pretty much none of the champions drop any pickups.
* {{I|Dream Catcher}} Doesn't show the outcomes for the boss waves and is bugged in the way that it doesn't show the right items, making it useless outside of the half-soul heart it gives each floor.
* {{I|Deep Pockets|r}}: Doesn't actually increase the amount of money you gain, causing it to only be valuable if you had a way to generate absurd amounts of money, which you don't need Deep Pockets to do.

=== Neutral items ===
* {{I|Sulfuric Acid|dlc=a+}} is both a blessing and a curse since it helps to always find secret rooms for free and destroy polyps; however it is bad for {{C|The Lost}} and {{C|Tainted Lost}} because they effectively can't hide inside rocks anymore.
* Both {{I|Head of the Keeper|dlc=a}} and {{I|Eye of Greed|dlc=a+}} are very useful throughout the entire run but are a severe disadvantage during the final boss fight, as it gives {{E|Ultra Greed}} and {{E|Ultra Greedier}} a consistent way to heal themselves.
* {{I|Member Card|}} offers more options for sale, however the items inside are still costly & indulging too much there may cause neglect of the base shop stuff.
* {{I|Magic Fingers}} and {{I|Golden Razor}} provide short-term helping hand at the cost of being less advantageous long-term.
* {{I|Money Power}} is a double-edged sword in the mode as it essentially forces the player to choose between buying shop items, or saving them for damage and the Greed Donation Machine.

== Notes ==
* With the nature of the mode's arena being the place most of the time is being spent at – anything that only temporary boosts up the character for one room is significantly more useful during the lingering battlefield. Penny-Related trinkets are also very useful with the constant flood of money.
* Despite being possible to make, red rooms will only open if a generated one is a special one, or if you're on the final floor. Red Rooms on the last floor are mostly empty with no contents inside. Some red rooms on the final floor can be Curse rooms or Super Secret rooms with some pickups in them.
* The combat room before Ultra Greed boss fight doesn't grant active item charges.
* Greed Mode is the only place in the game where {{I|Match Book}} doesn't drop {{T|Match Stick}}.
* Using {{I|Glowing Hourglass}} at the start of the run sends Isaac into the I AM ERROR room.

