== Trivia ==
* Ultra Greed's theme, named “Chorus Mortis”, is a remix of the main menu theme.
* Doodles that pop-up at the start of a run are always greed-themed in this gamemode.
* Isaac doesn't have the animation of jumping inside a golden chest in the end, possibly drawing a parallel with the ending in which he gets stuck inside a cave, drying up and becoming Greed. The updated Greedier ending also shows many spiders from isaac's body flooding up everything - drawing possible symolism of Isaac becoming rotten to the core.

== Bugs ==
{{bug|If the Super Secret Room is generated behind the locked (golden) Treasure Room, it is possible to get stuck by teleporting into before unlocking the Treasure Room. The Treasure Room doors all become unlocked when one of them is, unlike the normal game mode where a Treasure Room may have only one locked door, which results in the bombable wall between the Super Secret Room and the Treasure Room also being "locked". It cannot be bombed or opened with a key from inside the Super Secret Room, and unless another means of teleporting is available, the run is softlocked.}}
{{Bug|dlc=nr|The music played in chapters 1-4 have the wrong music. The music played will always be of the 2nd alt floor version of the current floor. For example, Burning Basement's track will play on Basement, and Flooded Caves's track will play on Caves.}}
{{Bug|dlc=nr+|Using {{i|Genesis|n}} forces you down a new "Ultra Greed" floor instead of the starting room, even if the final boss is already killed.}}
{{Bug|dlc=nr+|{{i|Dream Catcher|n}} shows the wrong items in Greed mode.}}
